{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STALE PREMISE — closing. My analysis window was behind `main`.\n\nVerified just now against both remotes:\n```\ngit show origin/main:src/rebar/_config_schema.py | wc -l   ->  677\ngit show gerrit/main:src/rebar/_config_schema.py | wc -l   ->  677   (cap 800)\n```\n\nA peer session had already split the file — change **1732** \"Restore the module-size gate\", merged as `ea6ee67e6a` — hours before I filed this. The 808 I measured was real at the commit my worktree sat on (`d2dea317ec`), but `main` had moved on, so both the breach and the \"blocks every lane\" consequence were already gone by the time I wrote them up.\n\nWhat was wrong with my method, worth recording because the ticket content itself was accurate: I measured the cap breach against my LOCAL HEAD and reasoned from `git log` on that same stale ref, then escalated without re-fetching. Every number in the growth table is correct for that commit and misleading about the world. A single `git fetch` before filing would have caught it — the check costs seconds and I skipped it precisely because the local evidence looked conclusive.\n\nThe one durable observation survives the retraction and is NOT recorded elsewhere, so repeating it here rather than losing it with the ticket: a file sitting at EXACTLY the cap is a trap for whichever lane adds the next key, and that lane usually cannot fix it either (I measured that trimming my own epic's entire footprint bottomed out at ~801). If a warning band on the module-size gate is ever considered, that is the argument for it.\n\nClosing as stale-premise, not as fixed-by-me: 1732 fixed it independently."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786653633324372001,"uuid":"0ef63629-2c64-4b76-b838-c8917a040d3f"}